            "review_title": "Review at Phung Vy - Hai San",
            "review_text": "bigyam77\nHong Kong, China94 contributions\n0\nStreet side Seafood goodness\nApr 2013 • Friends\nBeing from Hong Kong, seafood is something of a luxury usually involving carved carrot garnishes, much sizzle, if not much 'steak'. \n\nVietnam, on the other hand, has the blessing of abundant and delectable seafood right along its 1400km shoreline. And Phung Vy, an old standby amongst locals in District 10 HCMC, puts this abundant marine harvest to delicious use in a no nonsense casual setting (think flipflops and plastic stools by the street).\n\nAppetizers of oyster omelette, basil garlic mussels, steamed cockles, and fried garlic razor clams set the pace for a meal, making way for the big fish of ginger steamed roe crab, tamarind mud crab, and beer steamed flower crab. A 1kg grouper, steamed and with guts intact (Vietnam style), sits atop a metal plate on an open flame. \n\nThe vegetables are not the calling card but shine nonetheless. This is rounded off with an oyster congee (almost Chiuchow style) for a satisfying and very filling meal.\n\nIf there's a way you can fend off the non stop stream of local vendors (all very pleasant) hawking everything from cigarettes, shoe shines, lottery tickets and karaoke singing, that would be the icing on the cake!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 23, 2013",
